<title>ITALY: Specialists bid for 432 bln lire of Italy 5-yr BTP.</title>
<headline>Specialists bid for 432 bln lire of Italy 5-yr BTP.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for 432 billion lire of five-year fixed-rate bonds (BTP) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 200 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 4.359 trillion lire at the open auction for the January 1, 2002 paper, against two trillion lire worth of bonds on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 99.75 from 99.60 at the previous BTP auction on January 31.</p>
</text>
